  "units": [
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02760",
      "unit_index": 1,
      "source_text": "答诗故意模仿来诗。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "The reply poem deliberately imitated the poem that had been sent.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02760",
      "unit_index": 2,
      "source_text": "中纳言读给女御听了，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "The Middle Counselor read it aloud to the Consort,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02760",
      "unit_index": 3,
      "source_text": "女御说：“啊呀，使不得，恐怕她以为真是我作的诗呢。”",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "and the Consort said, \"Oh dear, that will not do; I am afraid she will think I truly composed the poem.\"",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02760",
      "unit_index": 4,
      "source_text": "她讨厌这首诗。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "She disliked the poem.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02760",
      "unit_index": 5,
      "source_text": "中纳言答道：“不打紧，看的人自能辨别。”",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "The Middle Counselor replied, \"It does not matter; anyone who sees it will be able to tell.\"",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02760",
      "unit_index": 6,
      "source_text": "便把信封好，交与女童。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Then she sealed the letter and handed it to the little girl.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02760",
      "unit_index": 7,
      "source_text": "近江君看了回信，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "When Omi no Kimi read the reply,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02760",
      "unit_index": 8,
      "source_text": "说道：“这首诗真好风趣啊！",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "she said, \"This poem is truly delightful!",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02760",
      "unit_index": 9,
      "source_text": "她在等待我呢。”",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "She is waiting for me.\"",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02760",
      "unit_index": 10,
      "source_text": "便用浓烈的衣香把衣服反复熏了几遍，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Then she repeatedly scented her robes several times with a strong clothing incense,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02760",
      "unit_index": 11,
      "source_text": "又用胭脂把脸涂得绯红，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "and used rouge to paint her face a vivid crimson,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02760",
      "unit_index": 12,
      "source_text": "再把头发重新梳过。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "then combed her hair all over again.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02760",
      "unit_index": 13,
      "source_text": "如此化妆，倒也另有一种华丽娇憨之相。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Made up in this way, she did have a certain splendid and charmingly naive appearance.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02760",
      "unit_index": 14,
      "source_text": "她和女御会面之时，想必还有许多笑话哩。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "When she meets the Consort, there will surely be many more amusing episodes.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
